    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0426" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/965</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-09-24T18:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 24, 6 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 25, 1914, 9 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>18. Informed confidentially Greek Minister has heard war between Greece and
                    Turkey imminent. Italy’s action problematical but weight of opinion is that she
                    cannot long continue neutral.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
